-- A2 — method-less impl inheriting a cross-module DEFAULT, at a head that ALSO
-- carries a same-spelled interface from a different module.
--
-- HAND-DERIVED EXPECTATION (DICT §8 I4: a class is (module, name); §5: the
-- interface default is used only when the SELECTED instance omits the method):
--   dtag Box -> di::Tag's default body            -> 7
--   otag Box -> other::Tag's explicit impl body   -> 100
-- Correct = (7, 100).
--
-- The other answer that would have counted: (7, 7) or (100, 100) = the two
-- same-spelled interfaces collapsed onto one route word.
import dimpl.{Box(..), dtag}
import other.{otag}

main = println (dtag Box, otag Box)
